Background

The Anderson thermostat applies a stochatic implusive force that acts occasioanlly on random selected particles, which effectively couples the system to a heat bath and maintain the system at a constant temperature. The coupling strength is determined by the stochastic collision frequency $
u$, and the distribution of time intervals between two successive stochastic collisions $P(t;
u)$ is in the Poisson form:
$$ P(t;
u)= 
u e^{-
u t},$$
where $P(t;
u)dt$ is the probility that the next collosion will take place in the time interval $[t,t+dt]$.
